# Igbo (ig-NG) -- hunspell affix file
# Windows LCID 1136.
# Character inventory from An Crubadan project metadata (CC BY 4.0).
# Onwu orthography. Tone usually unwritten in running text but written
# in teaching material, so it must not break tokenisation.
# The apostrophe is orthographic (n'ime, n'ihi) and is a word character.
LANG ig_NG
SET UTF-8
TRY aeiounbcdfghjklmprstwyzịọụṅñ́̀̄ńǹḿ

# Combining tone/dot marks must be word characters or hunspell
# splits words on them and never sees a whole token.
WORDCHARS ịọụỊỌỤṅṄñÑ́̀̄'’-ńŃǹǸḿḾ

# MAP relates a plain letter to its marked forms. This is what makes
# an undiacriticised input get the correct suggestion while still
# being rejected as wrong.
MAP 12
MAP i(ị)
MAP o(ọ)
MAP u(ụ)
MAP n(ṅ)(ñ)
MAP aáà
MAP eéè
MAP I(Ị)
MAP O(Ọ)
MAP U(Ụ)
MAP N(Ṅ)(Ñ)
MAP AÁÀ
MAP EÉÈ

# ICONV normalises input onto the exact forms held in the .dic.
# Generated from the wordlist: every letter-plus-mark cluster the
# dictionary contains gets a rule from its decomposed spelling, so a
# word typed with combining marks matches the precomposed entry. The
# vertical-line-below rules are a publishing convention, not a Unicode
# decomposition, so they are listed explicitly.
ICONV 28
ICONV Ị Ị
ICONV Ị̀ Ị̀
ICONV I̩ Ị
ICONV Ǹ Ǹ
ICONV Ñ Ñ
ICONV Ṅ Ṅ
ICONV Ọ Ọ
ICONV Ọ̀ Ọ̀
ICONV Ọ́ Ọ́
ICONV O̩ Ọ
ICONV Ụ Ụ
ICONV U̩ Ụ
ICONV ị ị
ICONV ị̀ ị̀
ICONV ị́ ị́
ICONV i̩ ị
ICONV ǹ ǹ
ICONV ń ń
ICONV ñ ñ
ICONV ṅ ṅ
ICONV ọ ọ
ICONV ọ̀ ọ̀
ICONV ọ́ ọ́
ICONV o̩ ọ
ICONV ụ ụ
ICONV ụ̀ ụ̀
ICONV ụ́ ụ́
ICONV u̩ ụ

# Deliberately NO IGNORE directive: making tone and dot marks
# ignorable would accept undiacriticised text as correct, which is
# the exact failure this dictionary exists to prevent.

# No PFX/SFX yet -- add them with a morphologically analysed wordlist.
